body:
The maintainer asked for a frontend code and design review that any fresh session can
repeat. The skill (.claude/skills/design-review) runs one cycle:
1. capture every surface at 1440 and 390 in fixture mode;
2. two fresh-context reviews: the pictures against DESIGN.md, and the code
   against the bugs that shipped;
3. browser-check every "broken" claim;
4. publish a gallery page for the maintainer's approve/veto comments;
5. file the approved fixes as a design-cN epic;
6. close with a handoff doc.
frontend/scripts/gallery.mjs takes the shots and writes a manifest with
page errors, console errors and sideways scroll per shot.
build_gallery.py turns a findings module into the page.
Proof: cycle 1 ran end to end on main: 18 shots; 27 design and 18 code
findings; 6 broken claims browser-checked (5 reproduced, 1 cleared);
gallery published. gallery.mjs fails fast when the server is not
answering.
